The rule is set up correctly. The badge will be inserted as the first child of `.preview-card-image-link`, which contains the stream thumbnail image. It will appear in the top-left corner of the stream preview image with an orange gradient background, making it prominent and easy to spot.

Here's what the "Top Live" badge does:

1. **Identifies top streams**: Scans all visible stream cards on the page and ranks them by viewer count
2. **Selects the top ~15%**: Streams in the top 15% by viewer count (or at least the top stream if there are very few) get the badge
3. **Displays a prominent badge**: An orange gradient "TOP LIVE" badge appears in the top-left corner of the stream thumbnail, styled with:
   - Orange-to-gold gradient background
   - White bold text
   - Subtle shadow for visibility
   - Positioned over the thumbnail image

The rule is idempotent - running it multiple times on the same element produces the same result, and badges are removed if a stream no longer qualifies as a top stream.

